    "narrative": "For today\u2019s matchup against Mikolas, **Bryce Harper** headlines the LawDog lineup as our top-rated play with a robust 78.75 score. His elite floor is anchored by a favorable park factor and strong peripheral xwOBA (.389), while a 25-PA BvP advantage adds a layer of confidence against a pitcher with a 4.77 xERA. Joining **Bryce Harper** in capitalizing on the favorable matchup are **Luis Arraez** and **Justin Crawford**; **Luis Arraez** benefits from an elevated spot in the order, while **Justin Crawford** serves as a vital weapon in our pursuit of stolen bases, overcoming a bottom-of-the-order penalty to maintain a 65.69 efficiency rating due to his high-ceiling speed profile. **Dylan Beavers** also profiles as an elite play today (68.38), benefiting from the leadoff spot and a high-leverage matchup against Johnson, R.\n\nThe primary bench decision for this slate involved **Gleyber Torres**, who sat just below our 40.0 floor at 37.78. While his #2 spot in the order provided a slight boost, the combination of a tough matchup against Miller, B (3.39 xERA) and negative park factors neutralized his potential, making the decision to keep him benched straightforward. Conversely, we are navigating risks with **Braden Montgomery** (40.02), who sits exactly on the threshold; his matchup against a tough southpaw in Suarez warrants caution, yet he remains in the lineup due to our current need for roster flexibility. We are also monitoring **JJ Bleday**, whose platoon disadvantage against Barnett suppresses his score to 47.64, and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who remains a staple despite a difficult draw against a high-skill arm in McLean, which forces his score down to 56.31 despite his undeniable pedigree.",
